 "conclusions": [
  "With the queue OFF on this image, burst still fails every latency target: invite p95 2397.7/2328, accept p95 1391.4/658.3, chat p95 5324.2/4738.3, health p99 124/102 and peer 162 ms. Queue ON (same image) gave invite p95 2238.1, accept 798.3, chat 4422.2: no meaningful difference. The earlier regression versus the 1733.9/767.0/4163.1 baseline is therefore not caused by the queue; it comes from other source/fixture differences since that image or run-to-run variance (not isolated here).",
  "During the ~8 s burst window both BFF containers sit at their 1-CPU cap (peak ~101-108%) while DynamoDB Local reaches 73-110% and Postgres/Redis stay under 20%. Whole-run means (30-40%) hide this. docker stats samples every ~2 s, so peaks are coarse. The burst is BFF CPU-bound (single-core cap), with DynamoDB Local near one core at the same time; Redis and Postgres are not limiting.",
  "Matrix on baseline image: steady, churn PASS (2/2 runs); ring-storm fails invite p95 305.4 and peer health p99 59.2 on group-four; double-accept fails health p99 54.5 only; soak fails chat p95 10263 and health p99 106/108.5. Burst fails. Capacity not accepted."
 ],
